# Copy to .env and fill in only if you want to. Axon runs fine with NONE of these set.
# With no .env at all, Axon uses its rule-based mock brain and stays fully offline.

# Optional. Free key from Google AI Studio: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# When set, Axon uses Gemini instead of the mock brain. See docs/adr/0005-gemini-brain.md
# — tested against a real key on 2026-08-03; re-verify the model name empirically if
# it's been a while, Google's free-tier model lineup moves.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional. Bigger embedding model = better recall, bigger download (1.2GB vs 134MB).
# AXON_EMBED_MODEL=thenlper/gte-large

# Optional. Where Axon keeps its database, vector store and checkpoints.
# AXON_DATA_DIR=./data

# Optional. Where Axon writes the real projects it builds for you (Step 8+).
# AXON_PROJECTS_DIR=./projects

# Optional. Used to build the `git push` URL for a GitHub note. `gh` (GitHub CLI) is
# not installed, so Axon cannot create the remote repo itself — create an empty repo
# on GitHub manually, named to match the project folder, before approving a push.
# GITHUB_USERNAME=

# Optional (Step 13). Sends real email for an "email <address> ..." note, only after
# approval. EMAIL_APP_PASSWORD is a Gmail "app password" (myaccount.google.com/
# apppasswords), NOT your real account password. Without both set, Axon still drafts
# the email safely and pauses for approval — it just can't send until these are here.
# EMAIL_ADDRESS=
# EMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
# SMTP_PORT=587

# Optional (Step 14). A Slack or Teams "incoming webhook" URL — both accept the same
# simple {"text": ...} JSON body. Without this set, Axon still drafts the message
# safely and pauses for approval — it just can't post until this is here.
# CHAT_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Optional (Step 15). Where Axon writes files for a "write/create a document" note.
# AXON_DOCUMENTS_DIR=./documents

# Optional (Step 12). The ONLY setting here that costs anything. Left unset,
# a GitHub-build note gets free placeholder files. Set to "claude" and approving
# such a note runs a REAL Claude Code build in that project folder, spending your
# Claude Pro plan's shared usage. Drafting/rejecting still costs nothing either way.
# AXON_BUILDER=claude

# Optional (Step 17). WhatsApp via Meta's Cloud API, free test-number tier: a test
# sender Meta provides, messaging up to ~5 numbers you verified in the Meta dashboard.
# WHATSAPP_TOKEN is a secret -- treat it like a password, and note the one the
# dashboard hands you expires in 24h (a System User token lasts indefinitely).
# WHATSAPP_TO is the default recipient: the number you verified, digits only with
# country code and no '+', e.g. 919876543210.
# WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=
# WHATSAPP_TOKEN=
# WHATSAPP_TO=
